            <ArticleTitle>Metabolic acidosis in the acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>106-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acid-base balance in 13 patients with acute abdominal conditions has been studied. Superior mesenteric arterial occlusion in 3 patients produced a base excess of less then-12. Other acute abdominal emergencies did not produce as profound a metabolic acidosis. The limitations of using severe metabolic acidosis as a diagnostic criterion in superior mesentric arterial occlusion are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
